<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sebastián Kindelán</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. <a href="/years/1826">1826</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Sebastián Kindelán y O'Regan</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sebastián Kindelán was a Spanish army officer of Irish descent who served as governor of East <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/florida">Florida</a> and later as captain general of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/santo-domingo">Santo Domingo</a> from 1818 to 1821. His rule fell in the period known as España Boba, when <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a> neglected the impoverished colony. He suppressed conspiracies against Spanish rule, but shortly after his term the colony declared independence and was occupied by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/haiti">Haiti</a>.</p></div>
